# appearance.allow — FORMAT constants under crates/kernel/src/video/ that appearance-check.py's colour shapes match
# but that no painter paints (APPEARANCE2, B473). One row per file + literal as written:
#   <path relative to video/ (a listed painter outside it reads ../<path>)>  <literal>  <reason>
# A u64/usize-typed or -suffixed literal is never a pixel and needs no row (PAINTERSCOPE, B482).
# A colour is never allowed here: it moves to video/theme.rs (a role fn, or theme::fixture for a selftest vector).
# A row that no longer matches the tree is STALE and fails the gate.
ceramic.rs      0x75AE_10B7     the grain hash SEED (a PRNG seed, not a pixel)
facet.rs        0x7FFF_FFFF     the PNG spec's 2^31-1 chunk-length bound
menubar.rs      [1,2,3]         KINDS, the three menu-extra kind ids, not an RGB triple
paper.rs        0xFBB6_0E9F     the paper grain hash SEED
paper.rs        0x9E37_79B1     the golden-ratio multiplicative hash prime (x)
paper.rs        0x85EB_CA77     the murmur3 fmix prime (y)
paper.rs        0x2C1B_3C6D     a hash avalanche multiplier
paper.rs        0x297A_2D39     a hash avalanche multiplier
paper.rs        0x68E3_1DA4     the per-octave hash offset
statusmenu.rs   u32::from_be_bytes([10,0,1,2])  the selftest's DHCP lease 10.0.1.2, an IPv4 address
vperf.rs        0x2000_0000     a 512 MiB BAR window bound (an address span)
wm.rs           0x165667B1      the xxhash32 PRIME32_5 in the window-identity hash
../arch/aarch64/display_tegra.rs  0x8000_0000  the DRAM floor a simple-framebuffer base must sit above (an address)
../arch/aarch64/display_tegra.rs  0x0003_0004  the aperture span that covers the FE cap word (a byte length)
../selftest.rs  0x9E37_79B9  the golden-ratio hash prime that fills the heap vector
../selftest.rs  0x1234_5678  the RwLock round-trip marker word
../selftest.rs  0xC0FFEE     the channel round-trip token
